        "notes" : "Locally modified vendored fork: Embedding-only Package.swift with library and build generator targets; Pinned fork build metadata, preventing accidental ancestor repository identity; Disabled debug Buffer.dump raw-terminal file logging; retained internal no-op method; Public renderer hooks and real implementation for font style permissions, pixel spacing, ligature shaping and cache identity; Render-only foreground theme remapping in dictionary\/plain\/underline\/caret paths without changing terminal cell attributes; Display P3 frame\/native\/Metal color path and cache\/surface\/backing-layer continuity; Configurable native and Metal cursor blink interval and visual-only forced cursor style; Render-only inactive pane background\/content multipliers; parser palette and OSC state preserved; Forced missing-face bold\/italic with native-face preservation, captured style permissions, fallback metadata and CG\/caret\/Metal cache identity; Rounded selection backgrounds in Core Graphics and Metal before independent inactive-content dimming; Optional fractional pixel viewport scrolling with overscan, hit-test\/caret alignment and warm row placement caches; Optional server-output-paced local resize reflow with requested backend dimensions retained before parsing; Shared cursor geometry and screen-correct NSTextInputClient anchors preserve marked-text alignment across fractional viewport scroll and resize without a visible native Metal caret; Host typography reflow preserves program modes and marked text while retaining only selections whose content survives reflow; Explicit blink suppression governs native CA and Metal without changing program cursor metadata; Font smoothing changes invalidate warm Metal row and glyph bitmap caches; Bounded native point-to-link accessor uses one terminal lock and the same Unicode and fractional-scroll hit testing as terminal mouse input; Explicit user\/protocol-response transport classification, bounded raw-writer process generation and deferred Kitty paste classification for host input ownership"
